OL,3,GNEWSARevived show made city feel like
OL,4,A'a big village'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe revival of a community show after a
OL,7,F15-year absence has made a city feel
OL,8,Flike "a big village", proud organisers
OL,9,Fhave claimed.
OL,11,FThe Durham City Show, which had been
OL,12,Frunning for at least 60 years before
OL,13,Fcoming to an end in 2011, returned on
OL,14,FSunday, showcasing vegetables, fruits,
OL,15,Fflowers, bakers and crafters.
OL,17,FCommittee chair Benedict Douglas said
OL,18,Fmore than 1,500 people attended the
OL,19,Fevent and hundreds of exhibits were
OL,20,Fentered into categories including
OL,21,F"rudest vegetable or vegetable
OL,22,Fdisaster" and heaviest apple.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
